{"id":"G3306","lemma":"μένω","transliteration":"menō","sayIt":"menō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to stay","meaning":"μένω,\n[in LXX for קוּם ,עמד, etc. ;]\nto stay, abide, remain.\n1. Intrans.;\n(i) of place: before ἐν, Luk.8:27, al.; παρά, with dative of person(s), Jhn.1:40, al; σύν, Luk.1:56; καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, Act.28:16; with adv., ἐκεῖ, Mat.10:11; ὧδε, Mat.26:38; metaphorically, 1Jn.2:18; of the Holy Spirit, Jhn.1:32, 33 14:17; of Christ, Jhn.6:56 15:4, al.; ὁ θεός, 1Jn.4:15, conversely, of Christians, Jhn.6:56 15:4, 1Jn.4:15, al.; ὁ λόγος τ. θεοῦ, 1Jn.2:14; ἡ ἀλήθεια, II Jo 2, al.\n(ii) Of time;\n(a) of persons: Php.1:25; before εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, Jhn.12:34, Heb.7:24, 1Jn.2:17; ὀλίγον, Rev.17:10; ἕως ἔρχομαι, Jhn.21:22, 23;\n(b) of things, lasting or enduring: cities, Mat.11:23, Heb.13:14; λόγος θεοῦ, 1Pe.1:23; ἁμαρτία, Jhn.9:41.\n(iii) Of condition: with pred., μόνος, Jhn.12:24; ἄγαμος, 1Co.7:11; πιστός, 2Ti.2:13; ἱερεύς, Heb.7:3; with adv., οὕτως, 1Co.7:40; ὡς κἀγώ, ib. 8; before ἐν, ib. 20, 24.\n2. Trans. (Bl., §34, 1; Field, Notes, 132): with accusative of person(s), Act.20:5, 23 (cf. ἀνα-, δια-, ἐν-, ἐπι-, κατα-, παρα-, συν-παρα-, περι-, προσ-, ὑπο-μένω).\n(AS)","glosses":["remains","remain","stay","stayed","abides","continue"],"count":102,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"and stay","kjv":"abide"}},{"chapterId":"mat-11","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"it would have remained","kjv":"it would have remained"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":38,"renderings":{"bsb":"Stay","kjv":"tarry ye"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-6","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"stay","kjv":"abide"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-14","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"Stay","kjv":"tarry ye"}},{"chapterId":"luk-1","v":56,"renderings":{"bsb":"stayed","kjv":"abode"}},{"chapterId":"luk-8","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"lived","kjv":"abode"}},{"chapterId":"luk-9","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"stay","kjv":"abide"}},{"chapterId":"luk-10","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"Stay","kjv":"remain"}},{"chapterId":